SLP vectorizer: limit the second-pass operand-chain vectorization to the register VF

Backport of three upstream llvm-project commits (dc6825047c42, 33578bd6698a and f77ec648706b; llvm-project #222755, #223016
and #223053). vectorizeNonVectorizableInsts() runs tryToVectorizeList() over every candidate set; with MaxVFOnly false and a
large candidate set (32 or more) the scan is quadratic. The added argument limits that second pass to the register VF.
Our trees still name the parameter LimitToRegisterVF, so the argument comment uses that name. The upstream test
(AArch64/operand-chains-max-reg-vf.ll) is not carried.

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Transforms/Vectorize/SLPVectorizer.cpp b/llvm/lib/Transforms/Vectorize/SLPVectorizer.cpp
index 28e665c..b23e6e9 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Transforms/Vectorize/SLPVectorizer.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Transforms/Vectorize/SLPVectorizer.cpp
@@ -33365,7 +33365,12 @@ bool SLPVectorizerPass::vectorizeNonVectorizableInsts(
   Changed |= tryToVectorizeSequence<Value>(
       Operands, OperandSorter, AreCompatibleOperands,
       [this, &R](ArrayRef<Value *> Candidates, bool MaxVFOnly) {
-        return tryToVectorizeList(Candidates, R, MaxVFOnly);
+        constexpr unsigned Limit = 32;
+        // Limit to StandaloneSeeds if !MaxVFOnly to avoid quadratic scan for
+        // large set of candidates.
+        return tryToVectorizeList(Candidates, R, MaxVFOnly,
+                                  /*LimitToRegisterVF=*/!MaxVFOnly &&
+                                      Candidates.size() >= Limit);
       },
       /*MaxVFOnly=*/true, R);
   return Changed;
